# "At the beginning of combat on your turn": Bishop, cast turn one, puts a counter on itself that combat (the control:
# the trigger does ask). Bot2's combat on turn two asks nothing (`! Bot1.Target`) and adds no counter. On turn three
# Bot1's trigger takes Bot2's Ornithopter as a target beside Bishop - "target creatures" are not limited to your own -
# and each gets a counter.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Mox Pearl
Agent Bishop, Man in Black
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Agent Bishop, Man in Black.Cast
Bot1.Target(Agent Bishop, Man in Black)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
! Bot1.Target
[T2 Bot2.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Agent Bishop, Man in Black.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Target(Agent Bishop, Man in Black; Ornithopter)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Agent Bishop, Man in Black.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 2
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 1
